Primary — your north stars (trust these)

Buyer uplift — extra unique buyers vs. control; the headline metric.
Order uplift — extra total orders/units vs. control; only diverges from buyer uplift once agents can buy multiples or bundles.

Diagnostics — track relative, not absolute (they tell you where uplift came from)

Click rate / CTR — % who clicked into the listing; moves when you change the image. (Your "buyer clickthrough rate" is the same thing — merge them.)
Read rate — % who actually read the description/reviews; moves when you change the copy.
Engagement rate — % who interacted beyond a glance (scroll, expand reviews, zoom images); define it concretely or it's noise.

Conditional — only if carts hold multiple items

Average basket cost — how much an agent's basket totals; useless in a single-product test, useful once you add cross-sell/bundles.

Sim-native — the stuff real analytics can't give you (highest value)

Dropoff-reason distribution — what share bailed for each reason; tells you why, not just that.
Objection-resolution rate — did your change actually kill the objection it targeted?
Per-persona uplift — who a change wins vs. loses, segmented by archetype.